at any kind of level
outside of a small circle.

00:29:57.586 --> 00:30:00.396
I don't know if it was an
article or a conversation,

00:30:00.396 --> 00:30:01.394
I don't remember.

00:30:01.394 --> 00:30:03.600
But I read something about the notion of

00:30:03.600 --> 00:30:08.383
that person or this story
I read was talking about

00:30:08.383 --> 00:30:12.248
becoming a caricature of yourself.

00:30:12.248 --> 00:30:14.060
And it really hit me, and
I was saying to myself,

00:30:14.060 --> 00:30:17.241
huh, am I forcing the narrative?

00:30:17.241 --> 00:30:20.352
Am I becoming more hyperbolized?

00:30:20.352 --> 00:30:22.209
More energetic?

00:30:22.209 --> 00:30:23.579
More intense?

00:30:23.579 --> 00:30:26.784
To pander to what the
audience is giving me.

00:30:26.784 --> 00:30:29.756
Am I becoming a caricature of myself?

00:30:29.756 --> 00:30:32.008
And I don't know if I've ever
really answered it, right.

00:30:32.008 --> 00:30:35.816
It was very difficult for
somebody that's really in tune,

00:30:35.816 --> 00:30:38.974
I was really struggling to
unpeel the banana and be like,

00:30:38.974 --> 00:30:39.995
Am I?

00:30:39.995 --> 00:30:41.017
Am I?

00:30:41.017 --> 00:30:43.038
It's interesting.

00:30:47.177 --> 00:30:48.895
What if it really happened, right?

00:30:48.895 --> 00:30:51.960
We just had a famous athlete
ask a question one second ago.

00:30:51.960 --> 00:30:53.585
What if

00:30:53.585 --> 00:30:55.791
Tom Brady hit me up and asked me?

00:30:55.791 --> 00:30:58.136
Would I be like, "Oh, Tom I wish you're

00:30:58.136 --> 00:30:59.344
leg fell off your body."

00:30:59.344 --> 00:31:02.409
The answer's no, I'm not that human right.

00:31:02.409 --> 00:31:05.288
And the truth is, it's actually
very hard for me to be upset

00:31:05.288 --> 00:31:07.354
with an athlete, even
though that's where I get

00:31:07.354 --> 00:31:09.188
sports muscles aka you guys know

00:31:09.188 --> 00:31:10.210
what beer muscles are right?

00:31:10.210 --> 00:31:11.255
Somebody get's drunk and they wanna fight.

00:31:11.255 --> 00:31:12.393
I get sports muscles.

00:31:12.393 --> 00:31:13.739
I'm at a sporting event, I wanna fight.

00:31:13.739 --> 00:31:16.038
But outside of it, especially right now

00:31:16.038 --> 00:31:17.803
in non football season,

00:31:17.803 --> 00:31:21.518
I feel like I'm almost
becoming a caricature of myself

00:31:21.518 --> 00:31:24.884
outside the football environment
of hating the Patriots

00:31:24.884 --> 00:31:26.719
and it was really interesting.

00:31:26.719 --> 00:31:28.762
I literally thought about that yesterday.

00:31:28.762 --> 00:31:30.852
So, being honest with myself,

00:31:30.852 --> 00:31:32.965
if he hit me up and asked me a question,

00:31:32.965 --> 00:31:35.937
I'd probably give him the best
sound advice that I could.

00:31:35.937 --> 00:31:38.166
And I'd try, 'cause
there's still a good part--

00:31:38.166 --> 00:31:39.443
as I was just about to say that

00:31:39.443 --> 00:31:40.581
(laughs)

00:31:40.581 --> 00:31:41.904
there was a part of my...

00:31:41.904 --> 00:31:42.926
(laughs)

00:31:42.926 --> 00:31:44.017
There's a part of me is
like, "This is the moment

00:31:44.017 --> 00:31:45.549
where I can finally put
the nail in the coffin

00:31:45.549 --> 00:31:46.548
and sabotage him."

00:31:46.548 --> 00:31:48.405
I mean, the truth is he's getting close

00:31:48.405 --> 00:31:49.520
to the end of his career.

00:31:49.520 --> 00:31:50.588
It's funny,

00:31:50.588 --> 00:31:52.608
Kobe, hated him my whole life.

00:31:52.608 --> 00:31:54.396
Like just hated him, sorry.

00:31:54.396 --> 00:31:57.020
But now I kinda root for him
because he's an underdog.

00:31:57.020 --> 00:31:58.529
I love underdogs, right.

00:31:58.529 --> 00:32:02.546
And I think Tom is the complete
and utter reverse of that

00:32:02.546 --> 00:32:05.030
in our society today and in my division.

00:32:05.030 --> 00:32:07.793
So it makes me very easy to dislike him.

00:32:07.793 --> 00:32:09.883
Look, he destroyed his phone,

00:32:09.883 --> 00:32:11.021
systematically

00:32:11.021 --> 00:32:12.739
to conceal the evidence.

00:32:12.739 --> 00:32:15.363
Nobody in public domain,
no matter what he does

00:32:15.363 --> 00:32:16.756
is going to believe him.

00:32:16.756 --> 00:32:19.705
So many people over and
over talk about the fact

00:32:19.705 --> 00:32:22.282
that people don't care
that much about the crime,

00:32:22.282 --> 00:32:23.954
they care about the coverup.

00:32:23.954 --> 00:32:26.926
It's unbelievable what America does

00:32:26.926 --> 00:32:29.526
with the coverup versus the actual crime.

00:32:29.526 --> 00:32:32.568
Literally probably right up to
where it gets to the ultimate

00:32:32.568 --> 00:32:34.658
like a murder, I don't
think we're like, all right.

00:32:34.658 --> 00:32:36.678
But underneath that, I mean there's like--

00:32:36.678 --> 00:32:38.582
I don't need to say 'em out loud.

00:32:38.582 --> 00:32:40.625
There's four to five things
in society that can be done

00:32:40.625 --> 00:32:43.922
where the issue is the issue.

00:32:43.922 --> 00:32:47.312
But boy, all those
thousands of other things

00:32:47.312 --> 00:32:49.704
they're actually things
we're more than willing

00:32:49.704 --> 00:32:52.699
to let go away because
we have all have empathy

00:32:52.699 --> 00:32:55.044
to know that we're not
perfect and we all have our

00:32:55.044 --> 00:32:56.576
skeletons in our closets.

00:32:56.576 --> 00:32:57.946
It's when you try to trick us

00:32:57.946 --> 00:33:00.500
after we, the collective United States,

00:33:00.500 --> 00:33:01.685
the collective world,

00:33:01.685 --> 00:33:03.263
have put you on such a pedestal

00:33:03.263 --> 00:33:05.562
and you've been rewarded with the riches

00:33:05.562 --> 00:33:07.211
that come along with that.

00:33:07.211 --> 00:33:10.113
And so I would say to him to have empathy

00:33:10.113 --> 00:33:12.644
and to understand why it's happened.

00:33:12.644 --> 00:33:16.614
And I would probably tell
him, which ugh it sucks

00:33:16.614 --> 00:33:18.147
but this is what I'd tell him.

00:33:18.147 --> 00:33:20.213
I'd probably tell him look, the truth is,

00:33:20.213 --> 00:33:22.140
the more you fight this, the worst.

00:33:22.140 --> 00:33:24.021
The more you approach it with empathy,

00:33:24.021 --> 00:33:24.857
it is what it is.

00:33:24.857 --> 00:33:25.855
The chips have fallen.

00:33:25.855 --> 00:33:27.736
You're probably too
emotional or passionate

00:33:27.736 --> 00:33:29.687
to apologize or admit.

00:33:29.687 --> 00:33:31.266
I don't think you have to do that.

00:33:31.266 --> 00:33:33.077
I think you just have to go neutral

00:33:33.077 --> 00:33:34.539
for a long enough period of time

00:33:34.539 --> 00:33:36.768
and I don't think anybody
cares 24 months ago--

00:33:36.768 --> 00:33:38.928
from now other than passionate Patriot

00:33:38.928 --> 00:33:40.762
and anti-Patriot fans that debate this

00:33:40.762 --> 00:33:42.318
for the rest of your career.

00:33:42.318 --> 00:33:45.313
Out of fondness of debating around sports.

00:33:45.313 --> 00:33:47.310
That's probably what I would tell him.

00:33:48.590 --> 00:33:49.585
That's it?

00:33:49.585 --> 00:33:50.149
- [India] That's it.

00:33:50.149 --> 00:33:51.264
- That's it.

00:33:51.264 --> 00:33:52.517
All right.

